<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Writing Inequalities to Represent Constraints</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00500</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Writing Inequalities to Represent Constraints</md:title>
    <md:uuid>ca53960f-bb99-4838-bd4c-ba2f07489414</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001">
      <title>Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">An elevator car in a skyscraper can hold at most 15 people. For safety
        reasons, each car can carry a maximum of 1,500 kg. On average, an adult weighs 70 kg and a
        child weighs 35 kg. Assume that each person carries 4 kg of gear with them.</para>
      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00002">Write as many equations and inequalities as you can think of to
            represent the constraints in this situation. Be sure to specify the meaning of any
            letters that you use. (Avoid using the letters <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>z</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>m</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>, or <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mi>g</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>.)</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00003">Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here are some
            samples:</para>

          <list id="list-00001">
            <item><m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>≤</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>15</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>, where <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math> represents the
              number of people in an elevator car.</item>
            <item><m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>≤</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>15</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>, where <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math> represents the
              number of adults and <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math> represents the
              number of children in an elevator car.</item>
            <item><m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>w</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>≤</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                  <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>500</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math>, where <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>w</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math> represents the
              weight in kilograms in one elevator car.</item>
            <item><m:math>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>w</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>70</m:mn>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>35</m:mn>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math></item>
            <item><m:math>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>70</m:mn>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>35</m:mn>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>≤</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                  <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>500</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math></item>
            <item><m:math>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>74</m:mn>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>39</m:mn>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>≤</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                  <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>500</m:mn>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math></item>
          </list>

        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->

      <!--Q#2-->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00004">After you have finished the following tasks, explain the adjustments
            you made to the equations and inequalities so that they are communicated more clearly.</para>
          <para id="para-00005">Trade your work with a partner and read each other’s equations and
            inequalities.</para>
          <list id="list-00002">
            <item>Explain to your partner what you think their statements mean, and listen to their
              explanation of yours.</item>
            <item>Make adjustments to your equations and inequalities so that they are communicated
              more clearly.</item>
          </list>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00006">Compare your answer: </para>

          <para id="para-00007">Your answers will vary.</para>

        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->

      <!--Text
      Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00008">Rewrite your equations and inequalities so that they would work for
            a different building where:</para>
          <list id="list-00003">
            <item>an elevator car can hold at most <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math> people</item>
            <item>each car can carry a maximum of <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math> kilograms</item>
            <item>each person carries <m:math display="inline">
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>d</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math> kg of gear</item>
          </list>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00009">Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here are some
            samples.</para>

          <list id="list-00004">
            <item><m:math>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>p</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>≤</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math></item>
            <item><m:math>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>≤</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>z</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math></item>
            <item><m:math>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>w</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>≤</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math></item>
            <item><m:math>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mi>w</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>70</m:mn>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>35</m:mn>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>d</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>d</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math></item>
            <item><m:math>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>70</m:mn>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>35</m:mn>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>d</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>d</m:mi>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>≤</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math></item>
            <item><m:math>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>70</m:mn>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>d</m:mi>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                  <m:mn>35</m:mn>
                  <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>d</m:mi>
                  <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>≤</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>m</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:math></item>
          </list>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    <section id="sect-00002">
      <title>Video: Writing Inequalities to Represent Constraints Solution </title>
      <para id="para-00010">Watch the following video to further explain the solution to the
        activity you just completed.</para>

